&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead quality and continuous improvement across the business to deliver reliable products, successful missions and customer confidence. Establish independent assurance, a scalable QMS and a leadership culture in which quality is built into every function. Enable on-time vehicle delivery at the agreed cadence through capable processes, credible readiness evidence and sustained improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer quality. &lt;/strong&gt;Own customer quality relationships, requirements, reviews, audits, complaints and escapes. Work with Mission Launch Operations as the internal customer for launch vehicles to define quality acceptance and handover evidence. Cascade requirements through Engineering, production, AIT and suppliers to raw materials; lead containment, corrective action and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product assurance. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead independent mission, project and design assurance from requirements through development, qualification, production and mission readiness. Establish assurance plans and gate evidence covering risks, traceability, interfaces, configuration, verification and validation. Challenge gaps and escalate unresolved risks to accountable decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;QMS and compliance. &lt;/strong&gt;Own the QMS across all business functions, including process controls, records, audits, management review and corrective action. Use AS9100 as the aspirational framework with a proportionate maturity roadmap. Coordinate compliance assurance with Legal and specialist owners, ensuring applicable contractual, regulatory and certification obligations have accountable owners and evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier and operational quality. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead quality assurance across suppliers, manufacturing, Propulsion AIT, Launch Vehicle AIT, engine testing and launch-pad AIT. Establish control plans, traceability and acceptance arrangements. Support current delivery and future product readiness, using AS9145 APQP as guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inspection requirements and quality at source. &lt;/strong&gt;Through the Chief Inspector, define inspection requirements, techniques and acceptance evidence with Engineering. With Production Engineering and Operations, maximise poka-yoke, automated checks and real-time in-process verification to prevent defects and drive right first time (RFT), reducing reliance on offline inspection. Validate controls against technical requirements; ensure capable methods, calibrated equipment, competent personnel and traceable results, retaining required independent acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem solving and learning. &lt;/strong&gt;Lead disciplined containment, root-cause analysis and corrective action for significant defects and escapes. Verify effectiveness, prevent recurrence and feed lessons from suppliers, builds, tests and missions into design and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lean management. &lt;/strong&gt;Own the business-wide Lean methodology, standards, capability development and maturity assessment. Equip leaders to improve their own functions through daily management, visual performance, standard work and structured problem solving, supported by specialist coaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous improvement. &lt;/strong&gt;Govern a prioritised business-wide improvement portfolio aligned with customer outcomes, delivery, quality, lead time and cost. Coordinate cross-functional learning and verify sustained benefits with accountable leaders and Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital thread and AI. &lt;/strong&gt;Connect quality and assurance evidence across PLM, ERP, MES, test and mission readiness. Apply AI and automation to analysis, document review, reporting and workflows to improve departmental efficiency, with trusted data, appropriate access controls and accountable human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Authority and working relationships&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chief Inspector. &lt;/strong&gt;Reports directly to this role and leads inspection capability and technical practice. Set priorities and assure the suitability of inspection methods, equipment and competence; Engineering retains authority for technical requirements and acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent quality authority. &lt;/strong&gt;Authority to stop work, contain material or withhold quality acceptance where conformity or required evidence is inadequate. Define escalation and disposition routes and provide independent visibility of risks to executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VP Spectrum Production. &lt;/strong&gt;Owns production teams, resources and execution. The Production System / CI Leader reports to VP Spectrum Production with a functional link to this role for methodology, standards, coaching capability and maturity assessment. Manufacturing and AIT leaders own local improvement delivery and sustainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director Spectrum Value Stream. &lt;/strong&gt;Owns end-to-end industrial delivery, customer commitments and Spectrum-wide production system performance through Block 2 and Block 4 Leads. Agree quality readiness priorities and improvement outcomes; provide independent assurance and evidence without assuming vehicle schedule accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering and Programmes. &lt;/strong&gt;Chief Engineers retain design authority and technical concession approval. Programme and mission leaders retain programme and mission decisions. Assure their processes and evidence, working with Production Engineering on process readiness, capability and design-for-manufacture feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Launch Operations. &lt;/strong&gt;Agree quality handover criteria and assurance evidence, communicate product risks early and close readiness gaps with delivery owners. Campaign command and launch authorisation remain with designated leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Planning and functional owners. &lt;/strong&gt;Align QMS controls with the business process architecture owned by Enterprise Planning and Transformation. Functions retain execution and compliance ownership; specialist teams retain their domain authority. Coordinate supplier quality with Procurement and local implementation with site leaders, including MD Sweden.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior quality leadership in space, aerospace or another high-reliability business, including multiple sites, product development and production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in customer quality, mission/project/design assurance, supplier and operational quality, QMS, audits and corrective action. Working knowledge of AS9100 and APQP principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to deploy Lean through leaders, coach improvement capability and deliver sustained gains across technical, operational and support functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical AI capability is required: demonstrable use of AI and automation to improve departmental efficiency, with measurable results. Experience with digital traceability and connected engineering and operational information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant technical qualification or equivalent experience; clear judgement, constructive executive challenge and a record of building capable teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aim radically high • Deliver, no excuses • Act with trust and integrity • Mission first, always&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Promote openness, early escalation and shared ownership of quality and improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Participation Program:&lt;/strong&gt; Share in our success through our virtual company share program&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days of vacation: &lt;/strong&gt;Enjoy the days off to relax and recharge &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company pension plan:&lt;/strong&gt; Secure your future with our company pension plan, featuring a 20% employer contribution after the probation period&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subsidised lunch:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay energised with delicious, subsidised lunches every day&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Flexible mobility budget&lt;/span&gt;: Travel your way with a choice between a fully financed Deutschlandticket, JobRad bicycle leasing, FINN JobAuto, or a fuel allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rental clothing with laundry service:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy hassle-free workwear with our convenient rental clothing and laundry service &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sport Clubs membership:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay fit with our sponsored sports club memberships (EGYM Wellpass)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning allowance:&lt;/strong&gt; Grow your skills with an individual learning budget granted after the probation period&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Childcare allowance:&lt;/strong&gt; Receive a childcare allowance for your non-school-age children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And Much More!&lt;/strong&gt; Discover additional perks and benefits when you join our team. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/jW2V5vsMb_k&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;314&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;We are Isar Aerospace and we are at the forefront of New Space building a modern space business to enable faster, better and cheaper access to space.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Our mission is to help democratise space and use it for good in order to improve life on Earth now and for the future generations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;We are a fast-growing company aiming to provide sustainable and environmentally friendly launch solutions for small and medium-sized satellites and constellations into Low Earth Orbit. The company is privately funded by world-leading technology investors with strong commitment and support and our team is made of driven and talented people with a real passion for space innovation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;We&#39;re making rockets in a way that hasn&#39;t been done before disrupting a traditional industry. If you are up for the challenge, want to work on cutting-edge projects and be part of a team changing the world for better, come, join us and launch your career!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Want to find out more about us?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;DE&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.isaraerospace.com/&quot;&gt;www.isaraerospace.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Protection&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We process your personal data for the purpose of managing the recruitment process and assessing your application. For detailed information on how your data is processed, including your rights, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://isaraerospace.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;DE&quot;&gt;Disclaimer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;DE&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot;&gt;Isar Aerospace SE is an equal-opportunity employer committed to fairness and inclusivity. We do not prioritize any specific religion, gender, nationality, or background. Due to security clearance requirements, affiliations with countries listed under § 13 para. 1 no. 17 SÜG may affect the application process. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Brief&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the enterprise planning framework that translates company vision and strategy, through commercial growth and customer demand, into aligned product development and operational plans. Bring together Commercial, Engineering, Programmes, Operations and Finance to create one funded, resourced and governed business plan. Lead the transformation, process architecture and resilience needed to deliver it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Role in Our Space Mission:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Enterprise planning — primary accountability&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision and strategy into plans: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate strategic objectives into a 3–5-year enterprise roadmap, annual business plan and rolling 36-month demand and delivery plan. Define planning assumptions, milestones, owners and dependencies across functions and sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial demand and growth: &lt;/strong&gt;Work with Commercial to translate customer needs, contracts, pipeline and growth opportunities into demand scenarios by product, configuration, launch date and site. Distinguish committed demand from probable and aspirational growth, making assumptions and confidence explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product development alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;Integrate the product roadmap, development priorities, engineering resources, qualification and test campaigns, configuration changes and industrialisation milestones. Reconcile customer needs and market timing with product readiness, including development demand competing with production capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations and capacity: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate launch demand into rocket, subsystem, supplier, manufacturing, integration, test and logistics requirements. Align workforce, equipment, inventory, footprint and launch infrastructure plans; expose constraints and define interventions, owners and required-by dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial reconciliation and choices: &lt;/strong&gt;With Finance, reconcile revenue, cost, cash, working capital and capital investment. Quantify demand, product and capacity scenarios; recommend prioritisation, make/buy, investment and timing decisions that balance growth, readiness and affordability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SIOP and execution linkage: &lt;/strong&gt;Implement monthly Demand Review, Supply and Capacity Review, Integrated Reconciliation and Executive SIOP. Connect 0–6-month execution, 6–18-month capacity and 18–36-month strategic planning to the longer-term roadmap. Baseline approved commitments, control changes and track decisions into delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Transformation and enterprise governance&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformation and process architecture: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the transformation portfolio required to execute the enterprise plan. Own end-to-end business process architecture, owners, interfaces and controls, aligned with the QMS and digital roadmap. Track milestones, adoption and verified benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk, continuity and governance: &lt;/strong&gt;Own business risk and continuity frameworks, impact assessments, recovery priorities and exercises. Establish weekly delivery visibility, monthly SIOP, quarterly enterprise/investment reviews and annual Board planning inputs, with clear escalation, decisions and action closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Required implementation outputs&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobilise the framework: &lt;/strong&gt;Agree the executive sponsor, process owners, calendar, common definitions, data sources, planning horizons, change rules and decision rights. Launch SIOP in parallel with development of the wider framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish the first integrated plan: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead a six-week mobilisation, targeting the first Demand Review within two weeks. Deliver a 36-month demand/launch plan, aligned development and rocket production plans, global capacity model, constraint and investment roadmap, and executive dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make it executable: &lt;/strong&gt;Secure functional ownership of assumptions and actions; present gaps, scenarios and recommendations for executive approval. Embed the plan in budgets, resource commitments and functional delivery reviews, with continuity gaps and recovery actions tracked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Checklist&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise planning: &lt;/strong&gt;Senior experience building integrated business planning or SIOP in aerospace, space or complex manufacturing. Proven ability to connect strategy, commercial growth, product development, operations and financial plans across functions and sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformation and resilience: &lt;/strong&gt;Track record in cross-functional transformation, business process architecture, governance and business continuity, including impact assessments, recovery planning and exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Judgement and leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong scenario modelling, capacity planning and financial understanding. Able to influence senior leaders, challenge assumptions and turn complex choices into clear decisions and accountable delivery. Relevant qualification or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI and digital capability — required: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrable practical use of AI and automation to improve departmental efficiency, analysis or planning, with measurable results. Experience connecting planning information across enterprise systems and maintaining reliable data and appropriate controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aim radically high • Deliver, no excuses • Act with trust and integrity • Mission first, always&lt;/p&gt;
